[{"location":"#imageGenerationWithDiffusionModels","page":"Home","title":"imageGenerationWithDiffusionModels","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"Documentation for imageGenerationWithDiffusionModels.","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"This Julia package implements a diffusion model to generate images of digits. It learns how noise alters the data and then predicts how to reverse this process to retrieve digits out of pure noise. This project can serve as a basis for more complex diffusion models.","category":"page"},{"location":"","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"","category":"page"},{"location":"#imageGenerationWithDiffusionModels.add_noise_to_image","page":"Home","title":"imageGenerationWithDiffusionModels.add_noise_to_image","text":"add_noise_to_image(img::Vector{Float64}, noise_step::Int64, alpha_bar::Vector{Float64}; rng = Random.GLOBAL_RNG)\n\nApplies Gaussian noise to an image.\n\nArguments\n\nimg::Matrix{Float32} : Input image\nnoise_step::Int64 : A noising step\nalpha_bar::Vector{Float64} : Vector of noise parameters. Length must be at least \"noise_step\". Comupted by taking the Cumulative product of (1-\"variance schedule\")\nrng::Random.TaskLocalRNG: Random number generator. Defaults to: Random.GLOBAL_RNG.\n\nReturns\n\nA noised version of image and the applied noise\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"#imageGenerationWithDiffusionModels.add_noise_to_image_old","page":"Home","title":"imageGenerationWithDiffusionModels.add_noise_to_image_old","text":"add_noise_to_image_old(img::Vector{Float64}, noise_step::Int64, alpha_bar::Vector{Float64}; rng = Random.GLOBAL_RNG)\n\nApplies Gaussian noise to an image.\n\nArguments\n\nimg::Matrix{Float32} : Input image\nnoise_step::Int64 : A noising step\nalpha_bar::Vector{Float64} : Vector of noise parameters. Length must be at least \"noise_step\". Comupted by taking the Cumulative product of (1-\"variance schedule\")\nrng::Random.TaskLocalRNG: Random number generator. Defaults to: Random.GLOBAL_RNG.\n\nReturns\n\nA noised version of image\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"#imageGenerationWithDiffusionModels.load_digits_data-Tuple{String}","page":"Home","title":"imageGenerationWithDiffusionModels.load_digits_data","text":"load_digits_data(filepath::String)\n\nLoads digits data from a .mat filepath.\n\nArguments\n\nfilepath::String: A filepath to .mat digits data.\n\n...\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#imageGenerationWithDiffusionModels.visualize_noising_of_image","page":"Home","title":"imageGenerationWithDiffusionModels.visualize_noising_of_image","text":"visualize_noising_of_image(img, noise_step, alpha_bar, rng = Random.GLOBAL_RNG)\n\nVisualizes the Gaussian noising process of an image.\n\nArguments\n\nimg::Matrix{Float32} : Input image\nnoise_step::StepRange{Int64, Int64} : Number of noising steps (in each step, noise is applied to the output of the previous step)\nalpha_bar::Vector{Float64} : Vector of noise parameters. Length must be at least \"noise_step\". Comupted by taking the Cumulative product of (1-\"variance schedule\")\nrng: Random number generator. Defaults to: Random.GLOBAL_RNG.\n\nReturns\n\nAn image visualizing the Gaussian noising process of an image horizontally.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"#imageGenerationWithDiffusionModels.FeatureEncoderNetwork._add_unet_level-Tuple{Vector{Tuple{Int64, Int64}}, Int64, Int64}","page":"Home","title":"imageGenerationWithDiffusionModels.FeatureEncoderNetwork._add_unet_level","text":"_add_unet_level(\n    in_out::Vector{Tuple{Int,Int}}, emb_dim::Int, level::Int;\n    block_layer, num_blocks_per_level::Int, block_groups::Int, num_attention_heads::Int\n)\n\nThis function adds a level to the UNet through the use of the ConditionalSkipConnection. The skipped layers are defined recursively until the intended level-count of the UNet has been reached. When the break condition is reached, the middle of the Unet is created\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#imageGenerationWithDiffusionModels.FeatureEncoderNetwork.make_down_path-Tuple{}","page":"Home","title":"imageGenerationWithDiffusionModels.FeatureEncoderNetwork.make_down_path","text":"makedownpath(; channels=(64,128,256), embdim=128, inch=1)\n\nReturns a tuple (encode, out_channels).\n\nencode(img, t_emb) : (latent, intermediates)\nout_channels :final channel count (needed by bottleneck)\n\nTODO: Visualize the intermediates of MNIST\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#imageGenerationWithDiffusionModels.Scheduler.cosine_beta_schedule","page":"Home","title":"imageGenerationWithDiffusionModels.Scheduler.cosine_beta_schedule","text":"cosine_beta_schedule(num_timesteps::Int, s=0.008)\n\nGenerates a noise schedule based on a cosine beta function.\n\nArguments\n\nnum_timesteps::Int : Number of timesteps.\ns : A variable, which varies the shape of the schedule. Defaults to: 0.008.\n\nReturns\n\nA beta schedule.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"#imageGenerationWithDiffusionModels.Embeddings.LearnedTEmbedding-Tuple{Integer}","page":"Home","title":"imageGenerationWithDiffusionModels.Embeddings.LearnedTEmbedding","text":"LearnedTEmbedding(dim; inner = 4*dim)\n\nTwo-layer MLP that maps a scalar time-step to a length-dim embedding vector.\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"},{"location":"#imageGenerationWithDiffusionModels.UNet.make_unet-Tuple{}","page":"Home","title":"imageGenerationWithDiffusionModels.UNet.make_unet","text":"Dummy Unet model\n\nDown-path  : built by make_down_path Bottleneck : #TODO Up-path    : #TODO\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"method"}]
